	"transcription": [
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:00,000",
				"to": "00:00:03,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 0,
				"to": 3880
			},
			"text": " This question comes from Vittorio, who asks, \"What if a glass of water was, all of a"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:03,880",
				"to": "00:00:06,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 3880,
				"to": 6360
			},
			"text": " sudden, literally half empty?\""
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:06,360",
				"to": "00:00:11,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 6360,
				"to": 11520
			},
			"text": " The pessimist is probably more right about how it would turn out than the optimist."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:11,520",
				"to": "00:00:14,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 11520,
				"to": 14880
			},
			"text": " When people say \"glass half empty,\" they usually mean a glass containing equal parts"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:14,880",
				"to": "00:00:16,080"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 14880,
				"to": 16080
			},
			"text": " water and air."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:16,080",
				"to": "00:00:19,200"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 16080,
				"to": 19200
			},
			"text": " Traditionally, the optimist sees the glass as half full while the pessimist sees it as"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:19,200",
				"to": "00:00:20,200"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 19200,
				"to": 20200
			},
			"text": " half empty."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:20,200",
				"to": "00:00:23,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 20200,
				"to": 23480
			},
			"text": " Linguist Gretchen McCulloch points out that \"we choose which reference state dimension"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:23,480",
				"to": "00:00:27,640"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 23480,
				"to": 27640
			},
			"text": " as a way to efficiently indicate whether the glass is currently being filled or emptied.\""
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:27,640",
				"to": "00:00:28,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 27640,
				"to": 28960
			},
			"text": " Language is cool."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:28,960",
				"to": "00:00:31,940"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 28960,
				"to": 31940
			},
			"text": " But what if the empty half of the glass were actually empty?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:31,940",
				"to": "00:00:32,940"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 31940,
				"to": 32940
			},
			"text": " A vacuum."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:32,940",
				"to": "00:00:35,140"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 32940,
				"to": 35140
			},
			"text": " The vacuum would definitely not last long."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:35,140",
				"to": "00:00:39,920"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 35140,
				"to": 39920
			},
			"text": " But exactly what happens depends on a key question that nobody usually bothers to ask."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:39,920",
				"to": "00:00:41,440"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 39920,
				"to": 41440
			},
			"text": " Which half is empty?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:41,440",
				"to": "00:00:44,440"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 41440,
				"to": 44440
			},
			"text": " For our scenario, we'll imagine three different half-empty glasses."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:44,440",
				"to": "00:00:49,000"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 44440,
				"to": 49000
			},
			"text": " The traditional air/water glass, a vacuum on top glass, and a vacuum on bottom glass."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:49,000",
				"to": "00:00:52,340"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 49000,
				"to": 52340
			},
			"text": " We'll imagine the vacuums appear at time t=0."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:52,340",
				"to": "00:00:55,060"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 52340,
				"to": 55060
			},
			"text": " For the first handful of microseconds, nothing happens."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:55,060",
				"to": "00:00:58,020"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 55060,
				"to": 58020
			},
			"text": " On this time scale, even the air molecules are nearly stationary."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:58,020",
				"to": "00:01:01,780"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 58020,
				"to": 61780
			},
			"text": " For the most part, air molecules jiggle around at speeds of a few hundred meters per second."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:01,780",
				"to": "00:01:04,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 61780,
				"to": 64600
			},
			"text": " But at any given time, some of them happen to be moving faster than others."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:04,600",
				"to": "00:01:07,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 64600,
				"to": 67320
			},
			"text": " The fastest few are moving at over a thousand meters per second."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:07,320",
				"to": "00:01:10,420"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 67320,
				"to": 70420
			},
			"text": " These are the first few to drift into the vacuum in the glass on the left."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:10,420",
				"to": "00:01:13,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 70420,
				"to": 73880
			},
			"text": " The vacuum on the right is surrounded by barriers, so the air molecules can't easily get in."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:13,880",
				"to": "00:01:17,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 73880,
				"to": 77120
			},
			"text": " The water, being liquid, doesn't expand to fill the vacuum in the same way that air"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:17,120",
				"to": "00:01:18,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 77120,
				"to": 78120
			},
			"text": " does."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:18,120",
				"to": "00:01:21,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 78120,
				"to": 81880
			},
			"text": " However, in a vacuum, it does start to boil, slowly shedding water vapor into the empty"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:21,880",
				"to": "00:01:22,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 81880,
				"to": 82880
			},
			"text": " space."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:22,880",
				"to": "00:01:26,040"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 82880,
				"to": 86040
			},
			"text": " The water on the surface of the left glass also starts to boil, but the incoming air will"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:26,040",
				"to": "00:01:28,380"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 86040,
				"to": 88380
			},
			"text": " stop it before it really gets going."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:28,380",
				"to": "00:01:31,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 88380,
				"to": 91680
			},
			"text": " After a few hundred microseconds, the air rushing into the glass on the left fills the vacuum"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:31,680",
				"to": "00:01:35,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 91680,
				"to": 95120
			},
			"text": " completely and rams into the surface of the water, sending a pressure wave through the"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:35,120",
				"to": "00:01:36,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 95120,
				"to": 96120
			},
			"text": " liquid."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:36,120",
				"to": "00:01:39,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 96120,
				"to": 99600
			},
			"text": " The sides of the glass bulge slightly, but they contain the pressure and don't break."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:39,600",
				"to": "00:01:42,640"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 99600,
				"to": 102640
			},
			"text": " Shockwave reverberates through the water and back into the air, joining the turbulence"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:42,640",
				"to": "00:01:43,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 102640,
				"to": 103840
			},
			"text": " already there."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:43,840",
				"to": "00:01:47,040"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 103840,
				"to": 107040
			},
			"text": " The shockwave from the vacuum collapse takes around a millisecond to spread out through"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:47,040",
				"to": "00:01:50,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 107040,
				"to": 110600
			},
			"text": " the other two glasses, which both flex slightly as the wave passes through them."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:50,600",
				"to": "00:01:54,800"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 110600,
				"to": 114800
			},
			"text": " In a few more milliseconds, the shockwave reaches the human's ears as a loud bang."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:54,800",
				"to": "00:01:57,800"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 114800,
				"to": 117800
			},
			"text": " And this time, the glass on the right starts to visibly lift into the air."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:57,800",
				"to": "00:02:01,640"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 117800,
				"to": 121640
			},
			"text": " The air pressure around the glass is trying to squeeze the glass and water together."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:01,640",
				"to": "00:02:04,000"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 121640,
				"to": 124000
			},
			"text": " This effect is easy to imagine with a wine glass."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:04,000",
				"to": "00:02:07,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 124000,
				"to": 127840
			},
			"text": " Air pressure at sea level is around 15 pounds per square inch, so in a typical glass, the"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:07,840",
				"to": "00:02:11,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 127840,
				"to": 131480
			},
			"text": " water's surface and the glass below it are being pushed down with a force of almost exactly"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:11,480",
				"to": "00:02:12,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 131480,
				"to": 132480
			},
			"text": " a hundred pounds."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:12,480",
				"to": "00:02:16,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 132480,
				"to": 136600
			},
			"text": " Normally, this force is opposed by the air pushing up on the bottom of the glass."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:16,600",
				"to": "00:02:21,040"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 136600,
				"to": 141040
			},
			"text": " But in the glass on the right, air pressure pushes the glass up from below on opposed,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:21,040",
				"to": "00:02:25,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 141040,
				"to": 145480
			},
			"text": " with a hundred pounds of force, while simultaneously pushing the water down from above."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:25,480",
				"to": "00:02:27,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 145480,
				"to": 147720
			},
			"text": " This is the force we think of as suction."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:27,720",
				"to": "00:02:31,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 147720,
				"to": 151600
			},
			"text": " The vacuum on the left didn't last long enough for the suction to noticeably lift the glass."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:31,600",
				"to": "00:02:34,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 151600,
				"to": 154840
			},
			"text": " But since air can't get into the vacuum on the right, the glass and the water begin to"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:34,840",
				"to": "00:02:36,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 154840,
				"to": 156480
			},
			"text": " slide toward each other."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:36,480",
				"to": "00:02:39,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 156480,
				"to": 159720
			},
			"text": " By now, the boiling water has filled the vacuum with a very small amount of water vapor."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:39,720",
				"to": "00:02:43,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 159720,
				"to": 163840
			},
			"text": " However, the glass and the water are moving too fast for the vapor buildup to matter."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:43,840",
				"to": "00:02:47,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 163840,
				"to": 167360
			},
			"text": " Less than 10 milliseconds after the clock started, they're flying toward each other at several"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:47,360",
				"to": "00:02:48,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 167360,
				"to": 168720
			},
			"text": " meters per second."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:48,720",
				"to": "00:02:52,440"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 168720,
				"to": 172440
			},
			"text": " Without a cushion of air between them, just a few wisps of water vapor, the water smacks"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:52,440",
				"to": "00:02:54,640"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 172440,
				"to": 174640
			},
			"text": " into the bottom of the glass like a hammer."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:54,640",
				"to": "00:02:58,440"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 174640,
				"to": 178440
			},
			"text": " Water is very nearly incompressible, so the impact isn't spread out over time."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:58,440",
				"to": "00:03:00,200"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 178440,
				"to": 180200
			},
			"text": " It comes as a single sharp shock."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:00,200",
				"to": "00:03:03,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 180200,
				"to": 183400
			},
			"text": " The momentary force on the glass is immense, and it breaks."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:03,400",
				"to": "00:03:07,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 183400,
				"to": 187240
			},
			"text": " This water hammer effect, which is responsible for the clunk you sometimes hear in old plumbing"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:07,240",
				"to": "00:03:10,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 187240,
				"to": 190520
			},
			"text": " when you turn off the faucet, can also be seen in the well-known party trick of smacking"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:10,520",
				"to": "00:03:13,000"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 190520,
				"to": 193000
			},
			"text": " the top of a glass bottle to blow out the bottom."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:13,000",
				"to": "00:03:16,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 193000,
				"to": 196400
			},
			"text": " In our situation, the forces would be more than enough to destroy even the heaviest drinking"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:16,400",
				"to": "00:03:17,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 196400,
				"to": 197400
			},
			"text": " glasses."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:17,400",
				"to": "00:03:20,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 197400,
				"to": 200600
			},
			"text": " In fact, when I was trying to calculate this, I bought a bunch of cheap glasses from the"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:20,600",
				"to": "00:03:24,040"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 200600,
				"to": 204040
			},
			"text": " dollar store and then tested, you know, applying different amounts of force to the base of"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:24,040",
				"to": "00:03:25,560"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 204040,
				"to": 205560
			},
			"text": " them to see how easy they were to blow out."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:25,560",
				"to": "00:03:29,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 205560,
				"to": 209520
			},
			"text": " And one of the glasses just didn't break no matter what I did, so I kept it, it sits"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:29,520",
				"to": "00:03:33,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 209520,
				"to": 213760
			},
			"text": " on my shelf, it doesn't match any of my other glasses, which kind of annoys me, and every"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:33,760",
				"to": "00:03:36,640"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 213760,
				"to": 216640
			},
			"text": " time I look at it, I think like, \"Thanks, science.\""
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:36,640",
				"to": "00:03:38,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 216640,
				"to": 218400
			},
			"text": " So this is why I stick to theory."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:38,400",
				"to": "00:03:41,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 218400,
				"to": 221240
			},
			"text": " The bottom is carried downward by the water and thunks against the table."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:41,240",
				"to": "00:03:44,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 221240,
				"to": 224760
			},
			"text": " The water splashes around it, spraying droplets and glass shards in all directions."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:44,760",
				"to": "00:03:48,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 224760,
				"to": 228880
			},
			"text": " Meanwhile, the detached upper portion of the glass continues to rise."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:48,880",
				"to": "00:03:52,200"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 228880,
				"to": 232200
			},
			"text": " After half a second, the observer's hearing of hop have begun to flinch."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:52,200",
				"to": "00:03:55,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 232200,
				"to": 235840
			},
			"text": " Their heads might lift involuntarily to follow the rising movement of the glass."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:55,840",
				"to": "00:03:59,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 235840,
				"to": 239600
			},
			"text": " The glass has just enough speed to bang into the ceiling, breaking into fragments, which"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:59,600",
				"to": "00:04:01,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 239600,
				"to": 241760
			},
			"text": " then return to the table."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:04:01,760",
				"to": "00:04:02,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 241760,
				"to": 242760
			},
			"text": " The lesson?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:04:02,760",
				"to": "00:04:06,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 242760,
				"to": 246840
			},
			"text": " If the optimist says the glass is half full, and the pessimist says the glass is half empty,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:04:06,840",
				"to": "00:04:08,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 246840,
				"to": 248240
			},
			"text": " the physicist shucks."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:04:14,760",
				"to": "00:04:19,200"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 254760,
				"to": 259200
			},
			"text": " [music]"
		}
	]
}
